  "changes": [
    "q310: Girl Talk bypasses trap setup; resolution bypasses trap-door lock.",
    "q310 lodge scene: bypass revenge invitation in both conversation entry paths.",
    "Ending boards: dual plays Yen then Triss; original single/none selection preserved.",
    "House: Yen intro then Triss intro; shared scene space is serialized; dual residents spawn together.",
    "House hotfix: Yen deactivation uses a hard-loaded community import, separate from the soft spawn reference.",
    "House residency hotfix: after leaving Triss behind, activate Yen directly; do not wait for distance to a despawned actor.",
    "House: both welcomes use retail layers and spawn phases; switch dual-only AP/anchor/trigger/furniture layers at the offscreen residency transition.",
    "Manor triss: native visit and single-romance phases retained; dual residency selects the dual layout. Legacy dual visit phase remains available for saved states.",
    "Existing-save migration: native terminal-pause deletion marker starts a fresh gated manor fix, including already-completed q705 saves.",
    "Manor reload: choose dual/native layers and community phases from both romance facts; retain native single-romance furniture selection.",
    "Ciri empress tavern: dual-only community/input/dialogue branch seats both companions at Geralt table; original single-romance branches retained.",
    "Q504 Triss community: added a dual-only phase/timetable; original single-romance phase remains unchanged.",
    "Single romances: native manor APs and routes retained, with geometry-identical path aliases for saved actions.",
    "Single romances: native dialogue trigger retained, with matching aliases for saved conditions.",
    "Q504 dual romance: independent Triss actionpoint at the existing third stool of Geralt/Yen table; native furniture and other actionpoints untouched.",
    "Q504 opening: dual-only input/dialogset with Geralt, Yen and Triss at the same table; native Yen lines retained; one dedicated three-person overview replaces the two-person shot. Single-romance inputs/timelines remain native.",
    "Manor: hidden dual-only world layer group; native spatial/furniture layers remain retail for single romances.",
    "Manor yen: native visit and single-romance phases retained; dual residency selects the dual layout. Legacy dual visit phase remains available for saved states.",
    "Triss: native chair actionpoint and staging moved together; separate route joins native outdoor path to the guest-room staircase.",
    "Triss repeat dialogue: independent world anchor; original voices, choices, cameras, poses and animation events unchanged.",
    "Triss dialogue availability: independent translated trigger, including cached world polygon and bounds; Yen trigger unchanged.",
    "Triss furniture: independent native lounge mesh, side table, jug and serving plate as streamed entities; original sector/furniture untouched."
